<title>CZECH REPUBLIC: Czech oil explorer Moravske 1996 net flat.</title>
<headline>Czech oil explorer Moravske 1996 net flat.</headline>
<dateline>PRAGUE 1997-03-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Czech crude oil prospector Moravske Naftove Doly a.s. said on Wednesday its 1996 net profit remained flat from the previous year at 31 million crowns.</p>
<p> Net profit (CZK million)   31.34    vs	  30.98</p>
<p> Operating profit	     48.79    vs	  64.74</p>
<p> Value of production	    n/a    vs     1,044.98</p>
<p> Total sales		 1,110.41    vs	 993.37</p>
<p> Total assets		1,354.50    vs     1,294.01</p>
<p> Basic capital		 834.26    vs	 834.26</p>
<p>Note. The company is an eastern Czech crude oil prospector and miner. Societe Generale holds a 40 percent stake in the firm. The Czech government privatisation agency, the National Property Fund, is the second largest shareholder with 31 percent. Moravske shares are traded on the parallel market of the Prague Stock Exchange.</p>
<p>-- Prague Newsroom, 420-2-2423-0003</p>
